WEBVTT

00:10:27.541 --> 00:10:30.356
You'll be familiar
with the double helix of DNA.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.896
Each rung contains information.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.493
So, DNA contains information
about how to make living organisms.

00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:39.979
And DNA also copies itself.

00:10:40.003 --> 00:10:41.209
So, it copies itself

00:10:41.233 --> 00:10:43.915
and scatters the templates
through the ocean.

00:10:43.939 --> 00:10:45.733
So the information spreads.

00:10:45.757 --> 00:10:48.395
Notice that information
has become part of our story.

00:10:48.877 --> 00:10:52.522
The real beauty of DNA though
is in its imperfections.

00:10:52.546 --> 00:10:56.474
As it copies itself,
once in every billion rungs,

00:10:56.498 --> 00:10:58.243
there tends to be an error.

00:10:58.267 --> 00:11:02.976
And what that means
is that DNA is, in effect, learning.